referenceAnswer.en:
Mock a unit's dependencies, never the unit itself. Remove the vi.mock and let the real implementation run:

```ts
import { it, expect } from 'vitest';
import { calculateTotal } from '@/features/cart/calculateTotal';

it('sums the cart line items', () => {
  expect(calculateTotal([{ price: 20 }, { price: 22 }])).toBe(42);
});
```

The general rule is the mutation check: mentally revert or corrupt the implementation under test and ask whether anything goes red. If the suite still passes, the test is worthless no matter what the tooling reports. Stryker automates exactly this check by injecting the mutations for you.

referenceAnswer.ru:
